Print enough of the firmware log ring to see why it died.

Each trapped thread dumps 8 lines, so a 25-line tail only ever showed ~3 idle
threads -- the firmware's own reason, "Error: ASSERTION FAILED main[565]: BOOTUP
FAILED. Check the GDB backtrace", always scrolled off. It appeared exactly once
in a 3.3 MB serial capture, by luck.

--- a/nss_log.h
+++ b/nss_log.h
@@ -45,7 +45,12 @@
  * This number should be lower than the minimum size of the logbuf
  * which 32 right now.
  */
-#define NSS_LOG_COREDUMP_LINE_NUM	25
+/*
+ * 25 was useless for diagnosis: each trapped thread dumps 8 lines, so the tail
+ * of the ring only ever showed ~3 idle threads and the firmware's own reason --
+ * "Error: ASSERTION FAILED main[565]: BOOTUP FAILED" -- always scrolled off.
+ */
+#define NSS_LOG_COREDUMP_LINE_NUM	250
 
